    {
      "id": "f8f37645-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 3,
      "content": "MAJOR INFORMATION The study of anthropology promotes an understanding of self and other by exploring the human condition at all times and in all places. In an interconnected world in which societies depend upon one another, failures in understanding and appreciating differences in goals, values and ways of life can lead to fear, discrimination, oppression, and war. The subfields of biological anthropology, archaeology, and sociocultural anthropology explore human evolution and the emergence of culture, cultural differences and similarities, regional history and ecology, and the role of language in culture. Students can earn additional first-hand experience abroad through participation in faculty-led programs , the California State University's International Programs , and independent field schools. ALL MAJOR REQUIREMENTS The complete list of major requirements is available here: http://bulletin.csusb.edu/colleges-schools-departments/social-behavioral-sciences/anthropology/anthropology-ba/ CSUSB ADVISING PODCASTS Find out more about this major here: What is the Anthropology Major? ASSOCIATE DEGREE FOR TRANSFER (ADTs) This major is similar to the Associate Degree for Transfer (ADT) in Anthropology. Completion of the ADT guarantees that students will be able to graduate from a similar-designated major at CSUSB in no more than 60 semester units. The ADT does not guarantee that all lower-division requirements are met. Community college transfer students with a compatible ADT MUST meet with an academic advisor early in their first term and each subsequent term to stay on track for graduation.",
      "contentHtml": "<h2>MAJOR INFORMATION</h2><p>The study of anthropology promotes an understanding of self and other by exploring the human condition at all times and in all places. In an interconnected world in which societies depend upon one another, failures in understanding and appreciating differences in goals, values and ways of life can lead to fear, discrimination, oppression, and war. The subfields of biological anthropology, archaeology, and sociocultural anthropology explore human evolution and the emergence of culture, cultural differences and similarities, regional history and ecology, and the role of language in culture. Students can earn additional first-hand experience abroad through participation in <a href=\"http://international.csusb.edu/StudyAbroad.aspx\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">faculty-led programs</a>, the <a href=\"http://csuip.calstate.edu/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">California State University's International Programs</a>, and independent field schools.</p><p><br></p><h2>ALL MAJOR REQUIREMENTS</h2><p>The complete list of major requirements is available here: <a href=\"http://bulletin.csusb.edu/colleges-schools-departments/social-behavioral-sciences/anthropology/anthropology-ba/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">http://bulletin.csusb.edu/colleges-schools-departments/social-behavioral-sciences/anthropology/anthropology-ba/</a></p><p><br></p><h2>CSUSB ADVISING PODCASTS</h2><p>Find out more about this major here:</p><ul><li><a href=\"https://csusbadvising.buzzsprout.com/1215218/10715826-ep-29-what-is-the-anthropology-major\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">What is the Anthropology Major?</a></li></ul><p><br></p><h2>ASSOCIATE DEGREE FOR TRANSFER (ADTs)</h2><p>This major is similar to the Associate Degree for Transfer (ADT) in Anthropology.</p><p><br></p><p>Completion of the ADT guarantees that students will be able to graduate from a similar-designated major at CSUSB in no more than 60 semester units. The ADT does not guarantee that all lower-division requirements are met.</p><p><br></p><p class=\"highlight\"><strong>Community college transfer students with a compatible ADT <u>MUST</u> meet with an academic advisor early in their first term and each subsequent term to stay on track for graduation.</strong></p>"
    }
